# SmritiSathi Knowledge Base

Reference for every Lovable prompt. Front-end only, mock data, no backend or real auth. When a prompt conflicts with this file, follow this file unless the prompt says otherwise.

---

## 1. Product Context

SmritiSathi is a mobile/tablet-first web app that helps elderly people with early to moderate dementia in North Eastern India (NER) keep their minds active, follow daily routines, and stay emotionally engaged. It gives caregivers and healthcare workers a simple way to monitor progress.

Many families live far from neurological care, so the app must feel **friendly, culturally familiar, voice-first, and usable offline**.

**Three views (mock role switcher at `/`):**

| View | Who | Core job |
|---|---|---|
| Patient | Elderly person with dementia | Play short games, confirm reminders, call for help |
| Caregiver | Family member of one patient | Set reminders, watch progress, answer alerts |
| Healthcare Worker | ASHA worker, nurse, clinician | Spot patients who need attention, add notes, set difficulty ceiling |

**Route map**

```
/                        Role switcher
/patient                 Reminder flow, then falls through to Home
/patient/home            Home (big cards)
/patient/play            Game picker
/patient/play/:game      Game screen
/patient/my-day          Today's schedule
/patient/family          Family photos and messages
/caregiver               Overview
/caregiver/reminders     Reminder list, add/edit drawer
/caregiver/progress      Trend charts
/caregiver/alerts        Alert list
/caregiver/settings      Language, voice, theme
/clinician               Patient table
/clinician/patient/:id   Patient detail
/clinician/alerts        All alerts
```

