## 4. Typography

**Fonts**
- Latin UI: **Atkinson Hyperlegible** (designed for low vision).
- Scripts and fallback: **Noto Sans** family, including Noto Sans Bengali (Assamese), Noto Sans Devanagari (Bodo), and Noto Sans Meetei Mayek (Manipuri).
- Font stack: `"Atkinson Hyperlegible", "Noto Sans", "Noto Sans Bengali", "Noto Sans Devanagari", "Noto Sans Meetei Mayek", system-ui, sans-serif`

**Type scale**

| Role | Patient view | Caregiver / Healthcare Worker |
|---|---|---|
| Page title | 40px / bold | 28px / bold |
| Section heading | 32px / bold | 20px / semibold |
| Body | 24px / regular | 16px / regular |
| Button label | 28px / bold | 16px / semibold |
| Caption | 20px minimum | 14px |

**Rules**
- Line height 1.5 for body, 1.25 for headings. Increase to 1.7 for non-Latin scripts.
- No italics or all-caps in the patient view.
- Left-align text. Never justify.
- Keep patient sentences under 12 words. One idea per sentence.

