## 6. Component Specifications

### Patient components
- **Big card** (Home): square-ish, large icon (64px+), one word label, 2 columns on tablet and mobile. Pressed state: gentle pulse plus soft sound.
- **Reminder card**: full-screen, illustration at top, one sentence, two stacked buttons ("Yes, I took it" primary, "Remind me later" secondary), speaker button to replay voice.
- **Home button** (sub-screens): fixed, large, labeled "Home" with a house icon, always the same position.
- **Speaker button**: round, 64px, always top right of the content area.
- **Timeline item** (My Day): large icon, time, short label. Done = green tick plus the word "Done".
- **Result screen**: 1 to 3 gold stars, one warm sentence, "Play again" and "Home".

### Caregiver and Healthcare Worker components
- **Stat card**: label, large number, small trend or hint line.
- **Side drawer**: slides in from the right (bottom sheet on mobile), title, form or detail, sticky action bar.
- **Table**: sortable headers, row hover, 10 rows per page. Becomes stacked cards on mobile.
- **Toast**: bottom center, 4 seconds, used for save and acknowledge only.
- **Sync chip** (header): see section 10.
- **Alert row**: icon, title, time, status badge (New, Acknowledged, Resolved, Will sync).
- **Skeleton cards** for loading. **Setup checklist** for empty state.
- **Confirmation dialog**: only for destructive actions such as deleting a reminder.

### States every screen must handle
Loading, empty, error, and offline. Patient loading = one calm spinner. Patient error = "Let's go back home" with one button. Professional error = short plain message plus a Retry button.

