## 7. Language and Tone

### Patient wording
Use short, warm, positive words. Address the person by first name.

| Use | Never use |
|---|---|
| "Good morning, Ama" | "Welcome back, User" |
| "Time for your morning medicine" | "Medication due" |
| "Nice try! Let's try again" | "Wrong", "Failed", "Incorrect", "Error" |
| "Great job today" | "Score: 40%" |
| "Let's go back home" | "Something went wrong", error codes |
| "Your family will appear here soon" | "No data", "Empty" |

**Game feedback rules**
- Encouraging only. No sounds that signal failure.
- After two misses, show a soft hint, never the answer in red.
- Stars always show at least one.

### Professional wording
Plain language, no jargon beyond what a nurse or ASHA worker uses. Use "Needs attention" and "Doing well" as the two summary labels. Avoid diagnostic claims. The app tracks engagement and cognitive activity, it does not diagnose.

